{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["And the sense of <b>the clean.</b> The ten mentioned, and all the others are unclean." "And the sense of <b>the unclean bird.</b> The one mentioned, and all the others are clean." "And the sense of <b>to defile.</b> That you shall know it is unclean in thought and in speech, and so you shall detest among the birds. Therefore a ger toshav may not eat unclean in a clean land, for on this condition does he dwell among us."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:11:26.744165669Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}